ev server proxies API requests to backend? Could just use CORS.\n\nLet's design:\n\nRoot directory:\n- package.json\n- package-lock.json? Will be generated by npm install. But we can create files then run npm install? We have write_file but no npm install tool. The environment may have npm. But the instruction says once dependencies declared in its package.json files are installed, npm run dev starts. So we just need to create files with correct dependencies. The test might run npm install then npm run dev.\n\nSo we need package.json files with dependencies.\n\nRoot package.json:\n{\n  \"name\": \"message-board\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"concurrently \\\"npm run dev --workspace=backend\\\" \\\"npm run dev --workspace=frontend\\\"\" ??? Might be simpler to just run concurrently directly with commands.\n\nAlternatively we can avoid workspaces, just have root scripts:\n\"dev\": \"concurrently \\\"npm run backend:dev\\\" \\\"npm run frontend:dev\\\"\"\nand define scripts.\n\nSimpler: create root package.json with devDependencies: concurrently. Then scripts:\n\"backend:dev\": \"cd backend && npm run dev\"\n\"frontend:dev\": \"cd frontend && npm run dev\"\n\"dev\": \"concurrently \\\"npm run backend:dev\\\" \\\"npm run frontend:dev\\\"\"\n\nBut concurrently runs in root, spawns child processes. That works.\n\nBackend package.json:\nname: message-board-backend\ndependencies: express, cors, @electric-sql/pglite\nMaybe also node types? Not needed.\n\nScripts: dev: node server.js (or src/server.js)\n\nFrontend package.json:\nname: message-board-frontend\ndependencies: vite\ndev: vite\nbuild: vite build\n\nWe need frontend source: index.html, src/main.js, maybe style.css.\n\nVite vanilla template expects index.html at root of frontend folder, with <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.js\"></script>\n\nWe need to ensure backend creates data directory for PGLite. PGLite needs dataDir option. According to @electric-sql/pglite docs: new PGlite(da